  "all_ingredients_flat": "chickpeas, onion powder, dry mango powder (amchur), Himalayan salt, Chaat Masala, sumac powder, black pepper, hot paprika",
  "instructions": "Rinse 1 can (16 oz) of chickpeas. Pat dry them thoroughly with a paper towel. Then transfer them to a baking tray lined with parchment paper. Add some Himalayan salt.\nPreheat the oven to 425 F. Roast the chickpeas in the oven until they turn crispy. Check them after about 15-20 minutes and toss them over. Then remove chickpeas from the oven.\nWe may add our favorite spices to roasted chickpeas. I added Chaat Masala, sumac powder, dry mango powder (amchur), onion powder, black pepper, and hot paprika.\nI let them stand for about 15 minutes before serving. Chickpeas were crispy & crunchy.",
  "cooking_methods": [
    "roast",
    "bake"
  ],
  "serving_suggestion": "I let them stand for about 15 minutes before serving.",
  "notes": "A recipe with BEANS (chickpeas), HERBS & SPICES (various).",
